## Pattern 11, share 13: yes posts

### They want a workable way to start potty training around the rest of family life.

15 of 179 posts.

Parents of two-year-olds and children approaching three ask where to begin, which rewards or equipment to use, and whether to train before or after a new baby. Pregnancy, travel, work schedules, another child's care and an antibiotic course complicate choosing a start date. Some have only introduced the potty; others are restarting after an earlier attempt or want a method that suits a sensitive child. A prospective relative foster carer also asks for basic toddler and potty guidance.

- "But then on the flip side if I wait until baby number 2 comes I might be too overwhelmed and it may be even harder to wait." [ar050-0001]
- "I bought the Hanes Boys' Potty Training Underwear, because we are planning on doing the cold turkey from diapers to underwear. But we don't have a full day or weekend to dedicate this to, based on our work and travel schedules." [ar044-0054]
- "I honestly don't even know where to start with potty training." [ar077-0001]
