### They have tried several ways to teach the potty and still meet refusal or indifference.

14 of 179 posts.

Parents of children from about two and a half to nearly four list rewards, books, timers, underwear, naked time and repeated breaks without a lasting change. They describe diaper preference, fear of the toilet or dirty underwear, indifference to wetness, and resistance despite strong language or other skills. One considers training a younger sibling first; others compare the difficulty with an older child's easier training.

- "But it’s getting discouraging that it’s been so long and so many attempts with literally no progress at all!" [ar028-0157]
- "She will only sit on the potty if she has a diaper on and she won’t go anywhere near the training seat we got for the toilet." [ar075-0088]
- "I bought her an incentive basket with just a bunch of Target dollar tree items. She wants the items but won’t go potty." [ar079-0047]
- "Naked doesn’t work, peeing every 10 min doesn’t work, somehow he just saves liquid to go on the floor." [ar024-0086]
- "Every time I bring up that seat she says ‘she is going to fall down’" [ar069-0212]

**But:** Refusal is not always complete inability to use the potty. "She is pretty good for poops and will usually poop in the potty." [ar075-0079]

