### They have made progress with pee but their child resists releasing poop on the potty.

15 of 179 posts.

Parents of children about two and a half through nearly four describe a separate hurdle with poop: fear, holding, waiting for a sleep diaper or wanting a nappy. Some children happily sit but cannot release; others will not approach, even when offered favourite treats. Parents weigh allowing a diaper against constipation and losing pee progress, and several say the child already has occasional potty poops.

- "She’s been pee potty trained since a little before her second birthday. We never separated poop from the process, she would just hold it in until it was awful and painful and beg for a pull up, or she’d wait til bed." [ar071-0008]
- "he now consistently only poops while asleep." [ar065-0076]
- "But her fear is outweighed more than her excitement for whatever the prize is." [ar054-0080]
