Parents of two- and three-year-olds describe poop accidents or no dependable potty pooping despite better pee use. Children may announce only after starting, not acknowledge stool at all, or finish once caught and moved to the toilet. The range includes twins approaching four, a child who shakes a dirty nap diaper onto the floor, and parents exhausted by cleaning soiled underwear.

