Parents of two- and three-year-olds describe withholding, pain or fear, tiny stool leaks, rashes and a daily routine dominated by toileting. They report laxatives, medical appointments, softening food and reassurance, sometimes without relief even when stools are soft. One parent describes a gastroenterology cleanout ending accidents; their general claims about other children remain that parent's account, not an assessment of these posts.

