### They want their child to notice the urge and stop playing before an accident.

5 of 179 posts.

Parents of children from two and a half to three and a half want body awareness and self-initiation rather than dry periods maintained by adult prompts. Children may know the words, describe what should happen, or show a pee dance but keep playing and wet themselves. Timers, rewards, games and reminders have not reliably produced a request before the accident.

- "The goal is intrinsic body awareness and self-initiation — not just compliance with external prompting." [ar080-0034]
- "He always informs us after he has started going that he is having “a pee feeling” and only had dry success if we are using a timer and bringing him to the potty." [ar071-0031]
