Parents of children about two and a half through three report screaming or refusal at public bathroom doors despite potty use at home or nursery. Noise, hand dryers or an unexplained new fear feature in the accounts. They have tried portable seats, ear defenders, modelling, encouragement or pull-ups, and want to manage necessary outings and even bathroom visits just to change a diaper.

